{"description":"Priority: P1 | Area: agent | Labels: chore, P1, area:agent | Milestone: v0.1.0 | RFC: TBD | Task: TBD

Define the architecture boundary for a future **headed Agent plugin** that consumes reusable `bitty-ai` infrastructure without being part of Wheel.

## Decision to record

Wheel remains a focused Coding Agent Harness: terminal/tool workflow, coding task graph, context, consent, audit, cancellation, and headless-first execution. The headed Agent is a sibling plugin, not a Wheel module and must not depend on `wheel.*`.

Both consumers use Bitty Core and `bitty-ai` contracts. `bitty-ai` owns reusable AI mechanisms and protocols; the new plugin owns chat/presentation/interaction composition.

## Design scope

Define ownership and versioned contracts for:

- Agent session/lifecycle and bounded text streaming;
- provider/model routing and capability/consent reuse;
- context/session snapshot boundaries;
- tool-call and approval events;
- Panel/Event Bus topics, focus/suspend/resume and multi-panel synchronization;
- TTS request/stream/cancel and audio resource limits;
- Avatar/2D/3D state, animation, viseme and bounded media-resource contracts;
- platform fallback for Linux, macOS, Windows and FreeBSD;
- security, privacy, queue, CPU/memory/GPU/audio budgets;
- an ownership matrix for Bitty Core, bitty-ai, Wheel, the headed plugin and optional media extensions.

## Non-goals

No Wheel implementation changes, no 3D/TTS implementation, no provider config loader, no Core Panel implementation, and no claim that the headed plugin is shipped.

## Acceptance

A self-contained canonical design document in `bitty-ai-docs` (not a research-only note), cross-repo contract references, explicit open questions and security review requirements, plus a decision that does not weaken existing Core/AI/Wheel boundaries. Independent architecture/security review is required before implementation tasks.","displayId":"AI-0343","id":"01M5KDNWN64F8S2QZTMCZWWNPM","priority":"high","status":"ready","title":"Design reusable bitty-ai contracts for a sibling headed Agent plugin"}
